<title>GERMANY: German government raises yield on 5-yr Bobls.</title>
<headline>German government raises yield on 5-yr Bobls.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government is raising the yield on its five-year Bundesobligationen bonds by lowering the issue price of the paper to 100.15 from 100.45, the Bundesbank said on Friday.</p>
<p>The move brings the yield on the Series 123 4-1/2 percent paper to 4.46 percent from 4.39 percent.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
